GUARDS THAT MUST HOLD
- Who can cause a join: only the existing gate. The asker's words name `org/name` in full, or the yes on the question (kept server-side, once, 15 minutes). A look-only key cannot (changes are refused before the action runs).
- Join only after the download worked (start), or after the repo is re-read on Hugging Face by code (`addModel`). Never from a search result.
- A failed join never fails a start. Nothing new starts, stops, claims or runs on a Spark; nothing on Spark 2; no SSH, Tailscale, firewall or access change.
- Card text is data: only code-block commands for that very repo are parsed; no card words reach the brain; flags, env and image pass `dig.vetSetup` at save and `resolveHow` at use (R27); a setup that lets the model run its own code is still never picked by `bestHow` and still refused by `start_model`.
- One fixed host (huggingface.co), no token, host never chosen by text that was read.
- added-models.json keeps one writer (`addModel`), found-setups.json one (`digModel`); no await between read and write (R20, R22).
- No page change, no new state file, no new event or job type, tool counts 24/37 unchanged.

ONE NEW ARGUMENT, NO NEW ACTION, NO NEW STATE. Tool lists and the 24/37 counts do not change. Proven on a scratch copy of the current tree (see `test`). Other builders are editing 16-actions.mjs right now, so anchor on the quoted text, never on line numbers.

WHAT IT RETURNS
`running_models {detail: "<container | spark/container | model name | repo | a word of the name>"}` returns only `{observedAt, textFromSparks, detail}`. `detail` is the list entry of that one running model (as `models[]` / `otherServers[]` give it today) plus: startedBySparkConsole, sparks (list), image, engine (vllm | sglang | trtllm | llama.cpp | null), command (list, secrets already `[hidden]`), contextTokens, contextSetBy, memoryShare (fraction or null), memoryShareGB, port, startedAt, setup ({id, recipe, source} or null), setupWords. Without `detail` the answer is unchanged. If `client` is passed too, `detail` wins and no paste card is built.

SOURCE (decided): one fresh `docker inspect <container>` on that one Spark through `run()`, parsed by the watcher's own `learnedFrom` (19-watcher.mjs). Not `knowledge.workloads`: the watcher re-inspects only when a container's id or state changes, so its `startedAt` goes stale after a restart, and it lags a start by up to a minute.

